{
  "version": "schemaxis.readiness/1",
  "routes": {
    "schemaxis.espeakng/1": {
      "guide": "docs/espeakng.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Turn a short plain-text script into a synthetic voiceover draft: a canonical PCM16 mono 22050 Hz WAV from the fixed offline eSpeak NG en-us voice or one explicitly selected voice (en-gb, fr-fr or es), proven by a fresh native re-synthesis of the captured text. Complements audio preparation (SoX), transcription (whisper.cpp) and archiving (FLAC), which cannot create narration. Unsuitable for human-quality voice, other voices, languages, variants or accents, translation, SSML or phoneme control, long scripts, and any claim of intelligibility, pronunciation or accessibility.",
        "assumptions": "A script of at most 1024 Unicode code points and 8 KiB, a literal string or an absolute local UTF-8 .txt file or artifact, within the documented Unicode profile, with native controls, markup and phoneme escapes refused. A configured eSpeak NG 1.52.0 espeak-ng executable with its matching native data; the host has no speech synthesizer. The finished narration must stay within 120 seconds and 8 MiB.",
        "constraints": "One operation, narrate. The voice (en-us unless the optional voice selects en-us, en-gb, fr-fr or es), pitch (50), amplitude (100), input encoding (UTF-8, -b1) and output (PCM16 mono 22050 Hz, 44-byte header) are fixed; only rateWpm (integer 120-240, default 175) and the optional voice are authored; an absent voice keeps the original en-us plans and receipts unchanged. Control characters, [[ ]] phoneme escapes, markup, text without a letter or digit, silent output and unsupported runtimes are refused. The narration is synthetic, not a human recording.",
        "inspection": "Inspect narration.wav (listen to it) and espeakng-summary.json (script bytes, SHA-256, code points and lines, requested voice with its listed name and file, rate, audio geometry and duration, PCM SHA-256, peak and nonzero samples, runtime identity and native-data fingerprint). verify needs the trusted espeak-ng (SCHEMAXIS_ESPEAKNG or a stored espeakng location; --espeakng belongs to run): it re-synthesises the captured text in a private directory and compares every PCM byte; there is no host speech synthesizer. Read the words as well as listening.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_ESPEAKNG_SOURCE: author exactly one of text and source; source is an absolute regular local .txt file. INVALID_ESPEAKNG_TEXT: remove the named control character, [[ ]] phoneme escape or markup, use UTF-8 and line feeds, and write at least one word. ESPEAKNG_BUDGET: shorten the script below 1024 code points and 8 KiB, or shorten or speed up a narration over 120 s or 8 MiB. ESPEAKNG_SILENT_OUTPUT: write words the selected voice can speak. ESPEAKNG_OUTPUT_REJECTED: the native WAV is not canonical PCM16 mono 22050 Hz; use eSpeak NG 1.52.0. INTERPRETER_NOT_FOUND: configure espeak-ng (--espeakng, SCHEMAXIS_ESPEAKNG or a stored location). UNSUPPORTED_RUNTIME: use eSpeak NG 1.52.0 with its matching native data and the selected voice listed exactly (en-us, en-gb, fr-fr or es): a runtime that lists another voice, or none, is refused rather than allowed to fall back. VERIFICATION_FAILED: the published bytes, retained evidence, JSON types, or the verifying runtime or native data differ; verify with the matching runtime and data or run again into a fresh directory."
      },
